All the versions of Moria are available by ftp from Kukulcan.Berkeley.edu

However, for those of you who do not have FTP capabilities, or find it
too much of a pain, I will distribute PC versions of Moria by diskette.

Now, I am not in the business of copying disks, so I would ask that you 
make it as easy as possible for me to distribute. I currently have the
B&W version 5.2.1 for 286/386 machines, the color version 5.2.2 for
286/386 machines, and the B&W version for 88/86 machines. I store them
each in an entire zip file (PKZIP version 1.10). To distribute them, I
unzip all the files from the desired version onto the appropriate disk.

I only have the above versions (includes manuals, etc, but no source code).
I only have 720K disk and 1.2M drives. Moria will not fit on a 360K when
uncompressed, and I obviously can't use a 1.44M disk.

If you want a copy, please send me the disk you want;

  --  720K 3.5" disk. These are less sensitive to handling abuse and,
      therefore, more desirable.

  --  1.2M 5.25" disk. If sending by mail, include a disk mailer or
      tape disk to a chunk of stiff cardboard.

  --  If you only have 1.44M 3.5" disks, send one of these. I will 
      reformat it to 720K, and load it. (A pain to me, so please try
      not to use this option).

  --  If you only have 360K, I will load it in zip format, with PKUNZIP
      version 1.10 (this is public domain S/W).

You *MUST* include a self-addressed stamped return envelope. If you can't
get to the post office, include a one dollar bill, and I'll buy postage
next time I go to post office for personal stuff (read "VERY long wait").
Either way, address your return envelope - I won't do that.

If you are in the University of Buffalo community or vicinity, drop the 
disk off in my Grad Student mail slot, across from the Mechanical Engineering
office on the 3rd floor of Gregory Jarvis Hall (North Campus).

Include a note, telling me which version you want. If you can, I would prefer
that you accept the disk in Zipped format. Then I dont have to unzip it for 
you. If you could do that, just write "zipped" on the note. I'll include
PKUNZIP 1.10 - I do not think previous PKUNZIP versions will unzip these 
files.

